# The `github` tool (design/agent-github.md, "PRs"; design/tool-contract.md,
# "One grant"): the std/go worker image with this directory's program curried
# onto it, plus the `help` it is described by. The github-token is granted to
# this image, and the other git tools mount it as DEEP-DEPS/github and hand it
# their remote work, so this one grant covers them all.
#
# A reader with no `@in`: its ArgTree is its arguments and nothing else, so
# `@request-id` makes each call its own run. A caller outside llm-step passes
# `--request-id=<any unused value>` itself.
HELP=<<END
Call the GitHub API at api.github.com with the granted github-token, or run a
batch of GitHub operations. Everything about a PR except its commits: find a
branch's open PR, open one, change its base, link PRs as a stack. Nothing is
checked out.

One call: method, path and optional body. The result is the HTTP status line,
then the response body, cut if long. A response of any status is a result; the
run fails only when none came back, and then a write may still have arrived:
read the affected state with a GET before sending it again.

A batch instead: batch is a JSON array of operations, run in order, stopping at
the first that is not ok. Each is one of:
  {"op":"api","method":"GET","path":"/repos/o/r/pulls","body":{},"ok_status":[404]}
    one call; ok on a 2xx status or one listed in ok_status
  {"op":"head","repository":"https://github.com/o/r.git","branch":"main"}
    the branch's commit as head, or null when it does not exist
  {"op":"push","repository":"...","commit":"<full hash>","branch":"topic","expected":"<full hash, or absent>","force":false,"allow_ignored":false}
    push the commit, leased on expected (the head you saw); ok when the branch is at the commit
  {"op":"import","repository":"...","revision":"main"}
    fetch a branch, refs/... name or full hash into caos; ok with its commit
The result is a JSON array, one object per operation: op, ok, error when it
could not be done, what it found, and skipped for those after a stop.

@param [method] GET, POST, PATCH, PUT or DELETE. With path; not with batch.
@param [path] API path with any query string, such as /repos/owner/repo/pulls?head=owner:branch&state=open. GraphQL is POST /graphql.
@param [body] JSON request body, such as {"title":"Add the parser","head":"parser","base":"main","body":"Why."}.
@param [batch] A JSON array of operations, described above, in place of method, path and body.
@request-id
END
curry --base:@=DEEP-DEPS/go --worker1:@=worker.go --help=$HELP
